{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'static pose|static weapon|static hat|Humanoid\\\\.pose|class Attack|class Shell|class Settings|class Audio|class Input|inputPreset|this\\\\.J =|J = \\\\{' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -50 && sed -n '650,685p' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '425,435p' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '1,95p' vendor/engine/src/assets/sets/adventure.js\"","aggregated_output":"754:class Input {\n3087:class Settings {\n4095:    this.sq = 0; this.sqV = 0; this.blink = 2; this.facing = 0; this.x = 0; this.y = 0; this.z = 0; this.J = {}; this._smear = null;\n4142:   *   E.Humanoid.pose's, tilt (radians: the whole body forward about the feet, a dive) and roll (sideways),\n4244:    const OW = this._ownW || (this._ownW = {});   // a game's own held poses (E.Humanoid.pose), eased in and out as state.pose names them, over the solve\n4795:/** held poses of a game's own (state.pose: an id), by id: E.Humanoid.pose(id, (J, w, rig) => ...) adds one */\n4874:Humanoid.poses = HUMANOID_POSES;\n4884:Humanoid.pose = (id, fn) => { HUMANOID_POSES[id] = fn; return fn; };\n4895:class Attack {\n9415:class Shell {\n- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n- `slash.active`: true while the strike can connect\n- `slash.busy`: true from the wind-up to the end of the recovery\n- `slash.cancel()`: stop the swing at once (hurt, dodged into)\n- `slash.hits(targets, test, fn)`: during 'active', call fn(target) once per swing for each target where test(target) is true. Returns how many were hit\n- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n- `slash.u`: 0..1 progress through the current phase\n- `slash.update(dt)`: advance the swing by dt seconds; returns the phase that began during it ('active' = play the swing sound), or null\n- `slash.hit`: the targets this swing has hit (each is hit once)\n- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n- `slash.spec`: the move: seconds of wind, active and recover, and its shape for the rig (a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, hitAt)\n- `slash.t = 0`: seconds into the phase\n- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n- `combo.active`: true while the current hit can connect\n- `combo.busy`: true while a hit of the chain is swinging\n- `combo.cancel()`: stop the chain; the next press starts it over\n- `combo.current`: the Attack of the current hit\n- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n- `combo.press()`: start or continue the chain. Returns true if a hit started\n- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n- `combo.update(dt)`: advance the current hit; returns the phase that began, as Attack.update\n- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n- `combo.moves`: the Attacks\n- `combo.step = -1`: the index of the current hit (-1 before the first)\n- `combo.window`: seconds after a hit ends that a press still chains\n- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }; E.Humanoid.hat adds one); weapon: 'sword' | 'gun' | 'staff' (E.Humanoid.weapon adds one); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair); draw: { under(g, Q, rig), over(g, Q, rig) } the game's own drawing before and after the body (Q: the joints on screen, [x, y, depth]: outfits, accessories); seed: its own random stream (blinks, its clock)\n- `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` †: a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h.g, h.rig\n- `E.Humanoid.hats` †: the hats a Humanoid may wear, by id: the built-ins (cap, band, crown, helmet, pointed) and a game's own\n- `E.Humanoid.pose(id, fn)` †: a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose names it or not (blended over the rig's solve)\n- `E.Humanoid.poses` †: the held poses of a game's own, by id (the built-in poses are the rig's own solve: state.pose names either)\n- `E.Humanoid.weapon(id, spec)` †: a weapon of the game's own (or a built-in replaced): { length: the tip's distance from the hand (a number, or rig => one; tip() and the swing's trail), rest: [forward, right, up] the way it points held at rest, blade: true (a swing smears along it), draw(w): its drawing in both styles (w.style, w.at(t), w.push(depth, fn), w.u: rig._weaponDraw) }\n- `E.Humanoid.weapons` †: the weapons a Humanoid may hold, by id: the built-ins (sword, gun, staff) and a game's own\n- `rig.debug(r)` †: skeleton overlay for debugging, draws straight into the buffer\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n- `r.ppu` †: pixels per world unit on the ground here: the view's scale times the zoom (iso 1.41, the others 1.5, overhead 1, at zoom 1). Rigs, maps and props grow with it; a sprite's pixel is a screen pixel at zoom 1 unless drawn with world: true\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\n- `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn, o = {})` †: queue a long piece of geometry (a wall, a fence, a roof's edge, drawn whole by fn(g)) a cell at a time from a to b ([x, y] world units) at height z, h tall: each cell-long piece sorts at its own middle, clipped to its part, with its box (as the engine's own walls are). o: queue's options, depth (its thickness across, 0), step (16 units)\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n/* adventure: a set of my-3D2dge's asset store (written by tools/asset-*.mjs; entries may be edited by hand).\n * The adventure starter's village stump and shrine obelisks (src/starter/10-adventure.js)\n * 2 shapes, 2 materials, 0 sprites. docs/ASSETS.md is the format; docs/ASSET-IMPORT.md how it was made.\n * \"sources\" records each download (its url, date, sha256 and license); an entry's src names its download, orig the file in\n * it, and fit how close it is: a shape's silhouette IoU at game scale (mean and worst view) and color dE.\n * Load it with E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['adventure']): its ids become 'adventure:id'. */\n(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {})['adventure'] = { set: 'adventure', format: 1, credit: 'The adventure starter\\'s village stump and shrine obelisks (src/starter/10-adventure.js)',\nsources: {'kenney-nature':{label:'Kenney Nature Kit',origin:'Kenney (kenney.nl), nature-kit',license:'CC0 1.0',url:'https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/nature-kit/37ac38a37b-1677698939/kenney_nature-kit.zip',page:'https://kenney.nl/assets/nature-kit',fetched:'2026-10-14',sha256:'fa7974a0d342bfe63c38664ba9f8ec1a4aab8ea25f099bdc56870e33588c4d9d',licenseHash:'cb96b75e3560ac78',dir:'nature-kit',scale:2.2,factors:'srgb'},'kenney-graveyard':{label:'Kenney Graveyard Kit',origin:'Kenney (kenney.nl), graveyard-kit',license:'CC0 1.0',url:'https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/graveyard-kit/ba8d4b4517-1760691807/kenney_graveyard-kit_5.0.zip',page:'https://kenney.nl/assets/graveyard-kit',fetched:'2026-10-14',sha256:'1a93613f2e5675f3310acf49ec9ef13ae7adeb756ac3b205bfb6cc9311a81062',licenseHash:'a48e274258386c6b',dir:'graveyard-kit',scale:2,factors:'srgb'}},\nmaterials: {\ncopper: '#e68458 bark',\nsteel: '#99a0c0 speck'},\nshapes: {\n'stump-round': {about:'round brown tree stump, flared base',tags:'stump forest',mats:{a:'copper'},parts:[['lathe','a',[0,0,0],[[0,0],[6.5,0],[5,2.5],[5,7.5],[0,7.5]]]],src:'kenney-nature',orig:'Models/GLTF format/stump_round.glb',fit:{iou:0.89,worst:0.84,dE:0}},\n'pillar-obelisk': {about:'stepped grey stone obelisk on a round base',tags:'decoration graveyard monument',mats:{a:'steel'},parts:[['box','a',[0.5,0.5,3],[9,9,1]],['box','a',[0,0,4],[8,8,16]],['box','a',[0,0,20],[6,6,9]],['box','a',[0,0,29],[4,4,2]],['box','a',[0,0,31],[2,2,2]],['cyl','a',[0,0,0],7,3.2],['cyl','a',[0,0,6.5],6,3.2]],src:'kenney-graveyard',orig:'Models/GLB format/pillar-obelisk.glb',fit:{iou:0.86,worst:0.84,dE:4}}},\nsprites: {\n}};\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
