{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '231,245p' vendor/engine/API.md && biome check --write src tools tests && ruff check tests/browser.py && node tools/test.mjs browser-input\"","aggregated_output":"| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\nChecked 13 files in 32ms. Fixed 1 file.\nAll checks passed!\nFAIL standard pad navigation/movement, glyph switch, hot devices, couch takeover and disconnect: Mouse aim did not transform through native camera\n4 passed, 1 failed (5 checks)\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from 'node:fs';import {createHash} from 'node:crypto';\nconst project=JSON.parse(readFileSync('project.json','utf8'));const files=['vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js','vendor/engine/LICENSE','vendor/hub/session.js','vendor/hub/harness.html','vendor/hub/bridge.js','vendor/hub/round.js'];\nconst dependencies=files.map(path=>({path,sha256:createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path)).digest('hex'),revision:path.includes('/engine/')?project.engineCommit:project.hubCommit,modified:false}));writeFileSync('docs/dependencies.json',JSON.stringify(dependencies,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconst p='../exit-interview.json';const data=JSON.parse(readFileSync(p,'utf8'));\ndata.testingFeedback=['14 game findings from automated tests and visual/code review were repaired; test-fixture and tool-configuration mistakes are excluded.','1 critical finding: Escape could strand the title screen. It is fixed and covered by a regression.','The ordinary-action complete expedition through the bundled HTML, independently checking all eight rooms, four recovered rings, four bindings, victory and replay.','Static reachability alone: useful for authoring, but unable to establish that a hero can execute the route or finish an extraction.'];\ndata.engineFeedback=['Native shaded Humanoid rigs, continuous Attack poses and material-defined objects give code-created art a consistent identity.','Yes: portrait coordinates and late Shell CSS initially caused blank portraits and crowded layouts; API/source inspection and screenshots resolved them.','The renderer-independent cooperative expedition simulation, companion utility behavior, checkpoint transactions and authoritative Hub adapter.','Coordinating native input/menu order, local joining, live session menus and independent simulation authority without changing collision during presentation.','none; the full pinned engine is unmodified. The game extends its shape, material, pose and UI registries.','A documented compact native-entity snapshot/restore adapter, including attack animation state and server-only examples.'];\ndata.promptFeedback=['The plan connects distinct hero roles, threatening geometry and ring extraction to a complete ending with concrete verification gates.','PLAN.md names an ultra configuration while TASK.md identifies max. TASK.md supplies this build’s metadata; an explicit completed filename example would also help.','Integrating the whole campaign, every input path, companion recovery and server-only authority into a portable single HTML file.','Keep the acceptance gates and add a minimal engine-plus-Hub shared-world fixture and a fully substituted delivery filename example.'];\ndata.sourceInformation.testing='Deterministic 120 Hz simulation; 40 ordinary extraction scenarios covering all ten pairs across four families at maximum Dread; normal complete campaign in simulation and final HTML; Chromium UI/controller/multitouch stand-ins; WebKit/Firefox native rendering; OfflineAudioContext signal checks; native asset sheets; AI Hub standard/lossy/departure/server/one-player conformance and shared gameplay. Physical devices, human listeners and human timing unavailable.';\nwriteFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconsole.log('Dependency checksums and complete interview saved.');\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
