 the full pinned engine is unmodified. The game extends its shape, material, pose and UI registries.','A documented compact native-entity snapshot/restore adapter, including attack animation state and server-only examples.'];\ndata.promptFeedback=['The plan connects distinct hero roles, threatening geometry and ring extraction to a complete ending with concrete verification gates.','PLAN.md names an ultra configuration while TASK.md identifies max. TASK.md supplies this build’s metadata; an explicit completed filename example would also help.','Integrating the whole campaign, every input path, companion recovery and server-only authority into a portable single HTML file.','Keep the acceptance gates and add a minimal engine-plus-Hub shared-world fixture and a fully substituted delivery filename example.'];\ndata.sourceInformation.testing='Deterministic 120 Hz simulation; 40 ordinary extraction scenarios covering all ten pairs across four families at maximum Dread; normal complete campaign in simulation and final HTML; Chromium UI/controller/multitouch stand-ins; WebKit/Firefox native rendering; OfflineAudioContext signal checks; native asset sheets; AI Hub standard/lossy/departure/server/one-player conformance and shared gameplay. Physical devices, human listeners and human timing unavailable.';\nwriteFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconsole.log('Dependency checksums and complete interview saved.');\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"Dependency checksums and complete interview saved.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_117","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'mouseGround\\\\(|clientToScreen\\\\(|screenToClient|mouseScreen\\\\(' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -25 && sed -n '1120,1149p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && rg -n 'mouseGround\\\\(' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | tail -8 && sed -n '2745,2765p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '1,115p' src/view/view.js && rg -n 'screen.*canvas|screen.clientTo' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_117","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'mouseGround\\\\(|clientToScreen\\\\(|screenToClient|mouseScreen\\\\(' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -25 && sed -n '1120,1149p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && rg -n 'mouseGround\\\\(' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | tail -8 && sed -n '2745,2765p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '1,115p' src/view/view.js && rg -n 'screen.*canvas|screen.clientTo' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"741:  clientToScreen(cx, cy) {\n1094:  mouseScreen() { return this.mouse.active ? this.screen.clientToScreen(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null; }\n2679:  mouseGround() { const m = this.input.mouseScreen(); return m ? this.view.toGround(m[0], m[1]) : null; }\n  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\n    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\n    else if (type === 'up') {\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\n      if (!o.touch) this.release('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._fed = null; this._gesture('up', x, y);\n    }\n  }\n  // a press followed from down to up: past 4 pixels it is a box (a left button, or a finger after a long press) or a pan\n  // (a finger, a middle or right button); lifted unmoved it is a tap, and a second within .35 s a double tap\n  _gesture(type, x, y, o = {}) {\n    const g = this._g;\n    if (type === 'down') { this._g = { id: o.id, x0: x, y0: y, x, y, t: this.clock, touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, mode: null, long: false, moved: false }; return; }\n    if (!g) return;\n    if (type === 'move') {\n      const px = g.x, py = g.y; g.x = x; g.y = y;\n      if (!g.moved && Math.hypot(x - g.x0, y - g.y0) > 4) { g.moved = true; g.mode = (!g.touch && g.button === 0) || (g.touch && g.long) ? 'box' : g.touch || g.button > 0 ? 'pan' : null; }\n      if (g.mode === 'box') this._gBox = { x0: Math.min(g.x0, x), y0: Math.min(g.y0, y), x1: Math.max(g.x0, x), y1: Math.max(g.y0, y), from: [g.x0, g.y0], to: [x, y], done: false };\n      else if (g.mode === 'pan') { const p = this._gPan || (this._gPan = [0, 0]); p[0] += x - (g.moved && g.panned ? px : g.x0); p[1] += y - (g.moved && g.panned ? py : g.y0); g.panned = true; }\n      return;\n2679:  mouseGround() { const m = this.input.mouseScreen(); return m ? this.view.toGround(m[0], m[1]) : null; }\n      this._raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);   // scheduled first, so an error never stops the loop\n      const raw = Math.max(0, (now - last) / 1000); last = now; since += raw;\n      // the refresh: the shortest of the last 90 frames (late ones are longer). Drawn every other refresh, only gaps shorter\n      // than one and a half are read (a GPU behind skips the refresh between: read, a 120 Hz screen would pass for 60); never\n      // the first, timed from start() and not from a refresh (it read 5 ms on a 120 Hz screen: 200 Hz until 90 more)\n      // and 90 long ones in a row, paced, mean the display slowed (a GPU behind lets the refresh between through some of the\n      // time): read afresh\n      if (raw > .004 && !fresh) {\n        if (this.drawEvery === 1 || raw < per * 1.5) { long = 0; ring[ri++ % 90] = raw; per = Math.min(...ring); }\n        else if (++long >= 90) { long = 0; ring.length = 0; ri = 1; ring[0] = per = raw; }\n      }\n      fresh = false;\n      const t0 = performance.now(), steps = this._run(raw), t1 = performance.now();\n      this.audio._frame(now);   // (the music clock between steps, and the sound held to it)\n      if (since >= (this.drawEvery - .5) * per) {   // drawn once drawEvery refreshes have passed (else a refresh left as it was: its updates have run)\n        n++;\n        try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); try { this.screen._present(); } catch (e2) { /* nothing to show */ } }\n        const st = this.stats, t2 = performance.now(); st.updateMs = t1 - t0; st.renderMs = t2 - t1; st.frameMs = since * 1000; st.steps = steps;\n        // a display at 90 Hz and up that the frames won't fit: every other refresh, back to each once they fit again. Two\n        // signs they won't: a frame's own cost, and refreshes missed between frames drawn at each (the GPU behind, which no\n        // clock here sees: that one holds 3 s, then 6, 12... up to a minute, before each refresh is tried again; 3 s again\n(function (G) {\n  'use strict';\n  const M = G.MA,\n    E = G.My3D2dge,\n    P = E.px;\n  class View {\n    constructor(game) {\n      this.game = game;\n      this.rigs = new Map();\n      this.positions = new Map();\n      this.remote = false;\n      this.master = M.masterRig();\n      this.keeper = M.heroRig('wizard', 1.1);\n      this.titleHeroes = [M.heroRig('warrior', 1.55), M.heroRig('wizard', 1.55)];\n      this.dragon = new M.DragonRig();\n      this.room = '';\n      this.epoch = -1;\n      this.lastEvent = null;\n      this.fx = [];\n      this.overlay = false;\n    }\n    rig(id, make) {\n      if (!this.rigs.has(id)) this.rigs.set(id, make());\n      return this.rigs.get(id);\n    }\n    visual(entity, key) {\n      const position = this.remote && this.positions.get(key);\n      return position ? { ...entity, x: position.x, y: position.y } : entity;\n    }\n    interpolate(entity, key, dt) {\n      const old = this.positions.get(key);\n      if (!old || !this.remote || Math.hypot(old.x - entity.x, old.y - entity.y) > 100)\n        this.positions.set(key, { x: entity.x, y: entity.y });\n      else {\n        const k = 1 - Math.exp(-dt * 19);\n        old.x += (entity.x - old.x) * k;\n        old.y += (entity.y - old.y) * k;\n      }\n      return this.visual(entity, key);\n    }\n    update(w, dt, title = false) {\n      this.master.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, facing: 1.4, pose: 'cast', expr: 'angry' });\n      if (w.room.rescue)\n        this.keeper.update(dt, {\n          x: w.room.cache.x,\n          y: w.room.cache.y,\n          z: 0,\n          down: w.cacheClaimed ? 0 : 1,\n          pose: w.cacheClaimed ? 'cheer' : 'down',\n          facing: 1.4,\n        });\n      for (const [i, rig] of this.titleHeroes.entries())\n        rig.update(dt, {\n          x: i * 30,\n          y: 0,\n          z: 0,\n          facing: i === 0 ? 0.4 : 2.7,\n          pose: title ? (Math.sin(this.game.time * 0.4) > 0.7 ? 'guard' : null) : 'cheer',\n        });\n      if (this.epoch !== w.epoch) {\n        this.epoch = w.epoch;\n        this.rigs.clear();\n        this.positions.clear();\n        this.fx = [];\n        this.lastEvent = null;\n      }\n      for (const source of w.heroes) {\n        const h = this.interpolate(source, `h${source.id}`, dt);\n        const rig = this.rig(`h${h.id}:${h.classId}`, () => M.heroRig(h.classId));\n        const pose = h.down\n          ? 'down'\n          : h.context && h.cmd.interact && ['revive', 'bind', 'cache'].includes(h.context.type)\n            ? 'binding'\n            : h.powerTime > 0\n              ? { warrior: 'guard', wizard: 'cast', phantom: 'stonewalk', changeling: 'mirrorcloak' }[\n                  h.classId\n                ]\n              : w.ring && w.ring.carrier === h.id\n                ? 'ringCarry'\n                : null;\n        rig.update(dt, {\n          x: h.x,\n          y: h.y,\n          z: h.z || 0,\n          vx: h.vx,\n          vy: h.vy,\n          facing: h.facing,\n          hurt: h.hurt < 0.4 && h.hurt > 0,\n          dash: h.dodgeTime > 0,\n          down: h.down ? 1 : 0,\n          pose,\n          attack: h.attack && h.attack.state,\n          expr: h.down ? 'wince' : null,\n        });\n      }\n      for (const source of w.enemies) {\n        const e = this.interpolate(source, source.id, dt);\n        if (e.dead) continue;\n        if (e.kind === 'dragon') this.dragon.update(dt, e);\n        else {\n          const rig = this.rig(e.id, () =>\n            e.kind === 'echo'\n              ? M.heroRig(e.copy || 'warrior')\n              : M.enemyRig(e.kind) || new M.NightmareRig(e.kind),\n          );\n          rig.update(dt, {\n            x: e.x,\n            y: e.y,\n            z: e.z,\n            vx: e.vx,\n            vy: e.vy,\n            facing: e.facing,\n            phase: e.phase,\n            pose: e.stun > 0 ? 'kneel' : e.phase === 'wind' ? 'cast' : null,\n            hurt: e.hurt > 0,\n250:- `game.screen.clear` †: true when the game's bg is null (or 'transparent'): the buffer and the canvas are cleared instead of filled, so a picture under the canvas shows through the game's (a 3D world [... omitted end of long line]\n251:- `game.screen.clientToScreen(cx, cy)`: browser client coords -> projected screen pixels (same space as view.p)\n252:- `game.screen.resize()`: fit the buffer to the canvas again (on window resize; after changing sizing options, setOptions does it)\n256:- `game.screen.OX = 0`, `game.screen.OY = 0`: the letterbox margins on the canvas, in canvas pixels\n257:- `game.screen.S = 3`: the whole-number scale up to the canvas\n259:- `game.screen.canvas`: the page's canvas (null in a headless game); o: the sizing options (the game's o)\n271:- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes fro [... omitted end of long line]\n300:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n310:- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n355:- `input.zones = null` †: areas of the screen a finger holds an action down in, [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }] (fractions of the canvas, 0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's tw [... omitted end of long line]\n592:- `E.diagnose(game = E.current)`: the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page, browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage [... omitted end of long line]\n794:- `map.chunks` †: the floor baked in squares of 128 screen pixels as the camera comes to them (its colors and the GPU lighting's canvas both), the far ones let go, so a 256 x 256-cell map costs what t [... omitted end of long line]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
