{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"agent_message","text":"Built **Much Ado About Rings**. Open [the game HTML](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-031651__x044b4b/work/Much-Ado-About-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-031651.html) in a browser.\n\n[Source and instructions](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-031651__x044b4b/work/Much-Ado-About-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-031651/README.md) · [Exit interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-031651__x044b4b/work/exit-interview.json) · [Progress](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-031651__x044b4b/work/PROGRESS.md)\n\n**59 checks passed**, including complete unassisted expeditions, forty class-pair extraction scenarios, controller/touch checks, and Hub multiplayer with server-only authority.\n\n**Source Information**\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Date / plan | 2026-11-06 03:16:51 / PLAN.md |\n| Source | [Quest for the Rings (1981)](https://odyssey2.info/library/library_view.php?i=53) |\n| Genre / perspective | Cooperative fantasy action-adventure; shared three-quarter view |\n| Tech | JavaScript/HTML/CSS; my-3D2dge 0.89.1; Hub Protocol 1, client 1.4.0 |\n| Art / animation | Original procedural pixel art; native skeletons, Attack timelines and custom rigs |\n| Audio | Code-only music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10% |\n| Online | Hub shared-world co-op; standalone solo companion and couch co-op |\n| Testing / research | Headless simulation, browser/input/audio checks and Hub harness; manual/scans and pinned engine/protocol documentation |\n| Environment / model | Codex CLI, headless Linux; OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, max |\n| Usage | added on import |\n\nPhysical-hardware results, first-time human duration, and original continuous music/timbres are **unknown**.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n\n1. 25 game findings repaired.\n2. Two critical findings fixed: title escape and malformed checkpoints.\n3. Most helpful: the bundled ordinary-action complete expedition.\n4. Least helpful alone: static path checks.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n\n1. Best feature: native rigs and material-defined art.\n2. Wrong guesses involved portrait coordinates, Shell CSS ordering and manual drawing.\n3. Main custom work: cooperative simulation, companion and network authority.\n4. Hardest integration: input, menus and live session simulation.\n5. Engine source changes: none; extended its registries and adapters.\n6. Suggested improvement: native entity snapshot/restore support.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n\n1. Clear cooperative pillars and completion gates helped most.\n2. PLAN’s ultra configuration versus TASK’s max configuration needed reconciliation.\n3. Hardest work: integrating the campaign, input modes and server-only hosting.\n4. Suggested improvement: provide a minimal engine/Hub fixture and fully substituted filename example."}}
